  "verbalization": "Tretamine is shown to have a target relationship with FaDu through two distinct pathways. In the first pathway, Tretamine targets Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2, mitochondrial, which is subsequently targeted by a specific compound, (1R,2S,4R,8R,10S,11R,13S)-11-hydroxy-2,11-dimethyl-7-methylidene-5,14-dioxatetracyclo[8.4.0.01,13.04,8]tetradecan-6-one, which in turn targets FaDu. In the second pathway, Tretamine directly targets Alpha globin, which is targeted by Ganoderic Acid K, also targeting FaDu. Both pathways suggest a potential mechanism by which Tretamine may influence FaDu, though the exact role of each intermediate compound remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible link between Tretamine and FaDu through these molecular targets, but further validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional relevance.",
